From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] mediatek: lcm: R63308_CASCADEMDZ40: give lcm_init a prototype

K&R-style empty parameter list in the Titan Pocket's reverse-engineered panel
driver:

  R63308_CASCADEMDZ40.c:318:13: error: function declaration isn't a prototype
      [-Werror=strict-prototypes]

The kernel's own top-level Makefile asks for -Werror=strict-prototypes, so this
is fatal rather than cosmetic. lcm_init takes no arguments; say so.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/lcm/R63308_CASCADEMDZ40/R63308_CASCADEMDZ40.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/lcm/R63308_CASCADEMDZ40/R63308_CASCADEMDZ40.c
@@ -315,7 +315,7 @@
 	params->dsi.ssc_disable = 1;
 }
 
-static void lcm_init()
+static void lcm_init(void)
 {
 	LCM_LOGD("%s enter\n", __func__);
 
